    "version": "Take 3 (Talk anywhere*)",
    "length": 56.98,
    "fps": 24,
    "width": 1280,
    "height": 720,
    "notes": "Talk anywhere*: a traditional 80s sell whose announcer the couple answer to the lens. Frank's confidence grows from the kitchen (Anywhere? Really? Anywhere?) to the patio, the mower and the roof, until he strolls backwards off the pool's edge. No splash shot: the fall cuts on his windmilling arms, the SPLOOSH and the fizz are heard on her red wall phone, and the punchline is him standing still, waist-deep and soaked: '...Honey?' fizz '...Anywhere?' Then our disclaimer card (fine print racing, very fast legal read) and tag card (ROAM PHONE, Talk anywhere*, $89.99, *at fine electronics stores everywhere, *almost anywhere). Every phone shot starts from the one approved handset still (roam3/stills/handset-b.png) or a still made from it; the handset is in his right hand throughout, and her red wall phone, in one locked framing, is the only cord. Each on-camera sentence is one generation; the announcer is Gemini TTS (voice Algenib). Cut by roam3/cut.mjs in the media folder from measured speech times."
  },
